Upstream:      rclone (github.com/rclone/rclone): cmd/serve/webdav/webdav.go,
               FileInfo.ContentType
Upstreamable:  yes, as an option rather than as is
How:           An issue and PR on rclone/rclone adding a serve webdav flag to
               take getcontenttype from the file name, as --use-server-modtime
               already does for getlastmodified. Changing the default would
               drop real content types for backends that list them.
Written:       2026-11-18, against rclone 1.76.0
Last checked:  2026-11-18
Remove when:   rclone serve webdav can answer a PROPFIND without reading each
               object's metadata, and the worker passes that option
Applied by:    packages/ceph-backup-worker/outputs.nix (the image's rclone only;
               the build fails if the patch stops applying)

A PROPFIND asks for each file's content type. For an S3 object rclone reads
it with readMetaData(), a HEAD request per object, since S3 listings carry no
content type. The worker reaches the Storj copy of the backup repository
through `rclone serve webdav` with kopia's flat layout, so every kopia
ListBlobs is a PROPFIND of the whole bucket: about 4000 HEADs. When Storj's
gateway answered HEADs in 0.3-1s (2026-11-16 to 18) a listing took 20 to 60
minutes, past kopia's 20-minute epoch refresh window, and kopia retried for
hours. The patch takes the content type from the file name, as rclone already
does for objects without one. Kopia does not read content types.

